## 3. Unit contract, original exposure and synchronization

**Q0/Q/q are eligible original ownership gons in this admitted mapping.**
The owner supplies documented original eligible gons, original wallet,
wallet-independent economic origin, original quote grouping, known ETH/DTF
components and evidence/snapshot identity. For a genuinely acquired principal
receipt, `Q0 = principalNative * originalOperationDivisor`; an incident or
live divisor cannot substitute for missing original-operation evidence.
For claim descendants, principal and reward allocations remain distinct and
cannot reuse the whole NFT contribution.

This is an acceptable source-normalization choice under plan sections
5.1-5.4 and PRD sections 6.2/8.2, not a claim that those requirements mandate
gons for every possible receipt mapping. Its basis is exact invariant
ownership associated with an explicitly allocated original exposure, not
merely the unit used by recovery inventory. There is no selectable pricing
mode. Current possession does not manufacture an original allocation.

Frozen `C0 = U(snapshot, ETH, originalEth) + U(snapshot, DTF, originalDtf)`
never changes with the live divisor. An ordinary funded rebase changes the
native redemption value of existing gons, not Q0 or C0. Separately issued role
gons cannot enlarge configured eligibility. No ancestry or special identity
for individual fungible gons is required; actual control plus the remaining
original cap is the boundary.

